*Experiment 8 - Write a C program that takes as command line argument the no. of megabytes of memory to consume that must memory observed during execution using free command*

- Create a C program named exp6.c - memory size in MB from command line & allocate the required memory using malloc()
- Complete the program `gcc exp6.c -o exp6`
- Run the program by providing the requirements - `./exp6 100`
- Observe Memory usage (free -h)
- Check the Program memory usage `ps aux | grep exp6`
- Release all allocated memory
- This allows the memory usage to be ... has terminated

